{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788313689788033001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"equitable-snazzy-fruitfly","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"1364999918c5b38ca5ea78497552a7127ef12d8b5bdd09cfd42873016a69f383","event_uuid":"76d9ecad-022c-478a-a21f-aa6944976938","position":{"commit_sha":"5f533282b0157655992e77ce7a03283cab509920","position":"1788311011421047001-76d9ecad-022c-478a-a21f-aa6944976938"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"142d883f81756d3f385c74c60523626c0f154c206ad328cfde972a45119bcc87","event_uuid":"b2f2dde2-a726-43db-820e-8c1d213e588e","position":{"commit_sha":"0b334c713bce1f0f28e4ea37cf3eb4e44c956502","position":"1788311037623819001-b2f2dde2-a726-43db-820e-8c1d213e588e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788311011421047001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nThe principal-engineer Janitor audit at snapshot `9a94ef9737fbdf070ae314bba6e797319aee2301` verified maintainability, oracle, documentation, compatibility, and dead-code findings that passed the fixed validity and impact floors and were approved by the maintainer. The audit itself changed no product code; this epic delivers the approved cleanup before further feature work consumes the recovered headroom.\n\nAuthoritative evidence and dispositions are in `.joe-janitor/report-2026-08-29.md` and audit ticket `literal-subaverage-dartfrog`.\n\n## Approach\n\nDeliver each approved remediation through a non-overlapping child whose plan owns its cited files and regression contracts. Structural extractions follow existing call-graph seams. Public removals state their replacement and breaking-change impact. Internal-only shim removal is gated by a prerequisite ADR and migrates every static, dynamic, string, test, and monkeypatch consumer before deletion. Reconciler compatibility removal is separately dependency-ordered so persisted state and live lock/exit contracts are migrated before old routes disappear.\n\n## Child Decomposition\n\n- Structural-headroom children own RP01, RP07, and RP13.\n- Behavioral-oracle and CI children own RP05, RP06, RP09, RP14, RP16, RP19, RP29, RP31, RP33, and RP36.\n- Adapter and documentation children own RP10, RP20, RP21, RP22, RP23, RP24, RP28, and RP35.\n- Public-deprecation and compatibility children own RP18, RP27, scheduled removals, config aliases, CLI aliases, the reconcile family, Python/MCP aliases, and MCP model re-exports.\n- The internal-shim container owns the prerequisite ADR and disjoint implementation shards, including SDC3.\n- Supplemental leaves own SDC1, SDC2, and SDC4.\n- RP02 and RP03 were already absorbed into completed `financial-stoneware-brant` work and are not duplicated here.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] [RP01/S13] Fsck repair planning, policy, restoration, pause, and application are separated along existing call-graph seams while abort semantics remain covered.\n- [ ] [RP05/O02] The config-surface golden rejects every unregistered live schema key and canonical environment name.\n- [ ] [RP06/O14] A behavioral oracle proves an effectful workflow step is invoked once and serially when it raises.\n- [ ] [RP07/S04] Only the MCP startup-handshake cluster is extracted, with lifecycle ordering and compatibility seams unchanged.\n- [ ] [RP09/O12/O13] Tests parse the shipped Docker stage and prove the health command opens the configured socket and fails on a bad response without requiring Docker in the normal test path.\n- [ ] [RP10/A06] Jira Cloud and Data Center delegate link normalization to one pure Jira-family canonicalizer while transports and provider-neutral diffing remain separate.\n- [ ] [RP13/S11] Independent table-driven LLM configuration readers leave `LLMConfig.from_env` as the sole precedence facade.\n- [ ] [RP14/T07] Pinned deployed Semgrep and Gitleaks integrations run in a portable direct-binary parallel Verified lane.\n- [ ] [RP16/O11/O07/O10] Sidecar stores use conflict-safe read-merge-write and observational concurrency/durability proofs.\n- [ ] [RP18/A13] Caller-selected reviewer inputs are removed from CLI, Python, MCP, and generated contracts before any billable call.\n- [ ] [RP19/S05] Production mutation builders emit create/parent ordering metadata and planner/dispatcher tests prove the order.\n- [ ] [RP20/C01/C02/C04/D06] Reconciler rollout, arbitration, configuration, and rollback documentation matches verified runtime behavior.\n- [ ] [RP21/C11/C12] Canonical review/gate descriptions are corrected and the existing MCP reference regenerated.\n- [ ] [RP22/D01] Maintained CLI guidance no longer advertises the removed `review` route.\n- [ ] [RP23/D02] Ticket types and statuses are generated from the canonical schema with drift checking.\n- [ ] [RP24/D05] Bug guidance documents claim-time exemption followed by post-RCA plan review for complex remediation.\n- [ ] [RP27/A11] The expired `REBAR_HLC=0` rollback branch is removed while legacy-event reads and clock injection remain.\n- [ ] [RP28/A12] Residual maintained severity-threshold guidance is removed and no operational config surface remains.\n- [ ] [RP29/O01] API snapshots include normalized return annotations and detect return-only drift.\n- [ ] [RP31/T02] The AST-identical blame-autoderivation test duplicate is removed without losing distinct boundary coverage.\n- [ ] [RP33/S16] Every third-party action in the privileged reconciliation workflow is full-SHA pinned and covered by existing security checks.\n- [ ] [RP35/S15] Git-backed `module_size_trend` and `cap_change_events` metrics implement the structured unavailable contract.\n- [ ] [RP36/O09] Truthful-tally tests require exact nonempty success output and reject empty output.\n- [ ] Scheduled public deprecations are removed with custom OpenAI-compatible Chat endpoints preserved.\n- [ ] All eight approved environment/config aliases are removed and canonical replacements are documented.\n- [ ] Simple CLI aliases are removed in favor of their canonical `bridge`/identity commands.\n- [ ] The complete `reconcile` and `reconcile-check` family is migrated to canonical bridge functionality, including persisted-state handling, then removed.\n- [ ] Python/MCP operation aliases are removed with their canonical replacements and breaking-change records.\n- [ ] Private MCP model re-exports are removed without changing MCP schemas or wire payloads.\n- [ ] A merged ADR prohibits internal-only compatibility shims while preserving deliberate public, wire, event, and persisted-data contracts.\n- [ ] Every inventoried internal shim consumer is migrated to its canonical owner and the old name/path is absent.\n- [ ] [SDC1] Dead reconciler retry/result residue is removed without changing live drift, lock-loss, bridge-exit, store-guard, or persisted-state contracts.\n- [ ] [SDC2] Superseded LLM workflow helpers are removed after their behavioral tests move to live owners.\n- [ ] [SDC4] Dead Jira adapter helpers are removed while mapper/codec and raw-PUT contracts remain covered.\n","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"none","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"Why no repository files change on this container: implementation and documentation edits are delegated to its child tickets. Where evidence lives: child ticket closure, their Gerrit changes, and this epic's acceptance criteria provide the completion record.","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["janitor","cleanup","code-health"],"ticket_id":"78f2-b104-e3c9-4b86","ticket_type":"epic","title":"Janitor Cleanup 2026-08-29","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["76d9ecad-022c-478a-a21f-aa6944976938","b2f2dde2-a726-43db-820e-8c1d213e588e"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788313689788033001,"uuid":"9f25546e-d28b-4cfb-aeed-3147c500a6ab"}